        summary: ['At high frequencies a cable is a transmission line with characteristic impedance Z0. A load that is not equal to Z0 reflects part of the wave: Γ = (ZL − Z0)/(ZL + Z0). The standing-wave ratio VSWR = (1 + |Γ|)/(1 − |Γ|) and the return loss −20 log|Γ| measure the mismatch.', 'A quarter-wave line transforms impedance: Zin = Z0²/ZL, so a λ/4 section of √(Z1·Z2) matches Z1 to Z2.'],
